### Component 4: Web Admin Panel Frontend

We will establish a modern, pluggable React web console inside an `admin-panel` folder in the root directory.

#### [NEW] [admin-panel/](file:///e:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/admin-panel)
A React TypeScript Vite project with a clean extension layout.
- **Pluggable Architecture:**
  - A core navigation sidebar loading screens dynamically.
  - An index route registry (`src/modules/index.ts`) allowing independent modules to plug in their layout, links, and views.
- **Core Screen Modules:**
  - **Auth Screen:** Secure login incorporating CAPTCHA image loading, OTP request, and verification.
  - **Dashboard:** Premium view of analytical counters (using gradient dashboard cards, micro-animations, glassmorphism cards).
  - **Users module:** Table list with search, user profile editor, and manual course purchase triggers.
  - **Purchases list:** Logs of transactions, provider types, and billing.
  - **Announcements & Banners editor:** Simple forms to add, edit, or delete items.
  - **Reports reviewer:** Filters to review and update student typos/feedback status.
  - **Audit Logs viewer:** Detailed chronological table of modifications.
- **Theme & Styling (`src/index.css`):**
  - Modern typography: Outfit / Inter Google fonts.
  - Visuals: Harmonious dark mode (deep blue/slate background, indigo accents, glassmorphic inputs, soft transitions, hover animations, responsive viewport).

